course: dictionary
lesson: 6755
title: Ooze: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. In «Honey oozed from the jar», ooze means to flow out slowly, because a liquid is moving.
explain: In «He oozes confidence», there is no liquid at all. Ooze means to show a lot of a quality. The word after it, confidence, is the clue.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense: «The monster oozed slime» works with "flowed out slowly", but «He oozed slime» would not make sense.
fact: Ooze can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it means to flow out slowly, or to show a lot of a quality.
fact: «Honey oozed from the jar.» Here ooze means a thick liquid flowing out slowly.
fact: «He oozes confidence.» Here ooze means showing a lot of confidence.
fact: As a noun, ooze means soft, wet mud, especially at the bottom of a sea, lake or river.
fact: In stories, ooze makes the reader picture something slimy or gooey, such as a monster or melted cheese.
exercise: «Honey oozed from the jar.» What does oozed mean here? | To shine brightly | *To flow out slowly | To crack into pieces | To jump high
exercise: «He oozes confidence when he walks on stage.» What does oozes mean here? | To sink into mud | To drip onto the floor | *To show a lot of something | To hide in a corner
exercise: «The divers sank into the ooze at the bottom of the river.» What is ooze in this sentence? | A type of boat | *Soft, wet mud | To show confidence | To flow out slowly
test: «The ladybird oozes yellow liquid from its legs when attacked.» What is the best swap for oozes? | Hides quietly | *Flows out slowly | Shines brightly | Grows very tall
test: Which sentence uses ooze to mean show a lot of a quality? | «The jar oozed honey onto the table.» | «The cake oozed chocolate from its middle.» | «The melted cheese oozed over the pizza.» | *«She oozed charm at the party.»
exam: «The echidna feeds its babies milk that oozes from patches of skin.» Which meaning of ooze fits best? | To shout loudly | To be very angry | To lose weight quickly | *To flow out slowly
